sprint: 117.14
title: Sync, Backup & Conflict Validation
date: 2026-09-30
canonical_objective: transfer, delta, retry, resume, encrypted backup, restore,
  conflicts, large assets, and workspace boundaries (external sprint_117.json,
  canonical sha256 b7ef2d350916951c52c5b444a01c51d4d1fd254e2569399b4b8b1f21820894d6)
verdict: SYNC_BACKUP_CONFLICT_VALIDATED_LOCAL

=== WHAT THIS STEP FOUND AND FIXED (shipped-code defect) ===
lib/features/collaboration/application/conflict_resolver.dart:33
  ConflictResolver.resolve walked `change.ours.keys`. A key that only the
  remote side changed is not a conflict, so no resolution was supplied for it
  and the key was never emitted. A remote edit was therefore reverted to the
  base value the user had already replaced, and a remote-only addition vanished
  with no trace. Silent loss of a synced edit.
  Fix: walk `change.changedKeys`; for a non-conflicting key, divergence decides
  (base != ours) rather than presence, and take the side that actually moved.
  Diff: 12 insertions, 5 deletions in one hunk.
  pre_fix_sha256: 42d6c2984d92ff0db231bf89f326a1403382ac7c551a32eba9752a1fe3ed81ec
  post_fix_sha256: a92da36b2b1b9d6af7080473e8d510427d0e203ea6d37fb9fd4c028c1e0b65e7
  RED: 5 pass / 2 fail, exit 1 (Expected '2' remote, Actual '1' base).
  Restoration used `git show HEAD:<path>` into a snapshot, never git reset/restore.

=== SECOND, NON-OBVIOUS DEFECT (cross-step measurement) ===
lib/features/world_logic/domain/sprint_117_global_scope_workspace_boundary_validation.dart:1107
  117.11's `_callSites(symbol)` decides "is this gate called by shipped code?"
  by scanning lib/ and excluding only ITS OWN family by hardcoded name
  (`sprint_117_global_scope`). Every other step's acceptance harness therefore
  counted as a PRODUCTION CALLER. Adding 117.14's drill - which legitimately
  drills the same AccountCenterWorkspaceBoundaryContract - made 117.11 report a
  production caller that does not exist and flipped its `unresolvable` verdict.
  Reproduction (cause isolated, not guessed):
    with 117.14 drill+validation moved out of lib/ -> 117.11 = 30/30 exit 0
    with them present                          -> 117.11 = 5 failures, exit 1
  Fix: exclude every `sprint_117_*` harness from the production-caller count.
  No sprint_117_* file is reachable from main.dart, so none is production wiring.
  VALIDATED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS (a blanket exclusion that silences the check
  would be worse than the bug):
    - a genuine caller in a non-harness file (lib/features/collaboration/
      application/_poison_callsite.dart, TEMPORARY probe, real call to
      resolveTransfer) still flips the counter and fails 117.11 -> the check
      still bites. Probe removed in the same run; no residue.
    - with no genuine caller, 117.11 is 30/30 again.

