=== WINDOWS BUILD SCOPE (HONEST, same discipline as 117.13) ===
  The debug build CANNOT attest this slice. Forced recompile did produce a
  fresh app.dill (mtime 2026-09-30 22:02:11), yet symbol counts in it are:
    ConflictResolver 0, SyncChangeSet 0, Sprint117SyncBackupConflictDrill 0,
    CloudStorageAggregation 0, but CONTROL StorageUsageCard 20.
  => the collaboration/sync chain is not reachable from main.dart, exactly as
  117.12 and 117.13 were. The control symbol proves the counting method works.
  WHAT THE BUILD DOES establish: no regression to the reachable program
  (native assets, CMake, MSBuild, plugins) at this HEAD + slice.
  WHAT IT DOES NOT establish: that the changed Dart was compiled into the
  debug kernel. Real coverage is the focused/shard runs, which compile these
  files directly and were measured with necessity in both directions.

=== ACCEPTANCE NOT SATISFIABLE BY SHIPPED CODE (recorded, not folded into pass) ===
  No shipped code performs a sync. FolderCloudSyncService round-trips a whole
  project map through one JSON file per project: no delta protocol, no chunked
  or streamed transfer, no encrypted-archive writer, no retry against a real
  endpoint anywhere in lib/.
  The gate therefore records, as acceptance_unmet with exact reasons:
    delta, encrypted_backup (no archive writer; encryption is a declared
    field no shipped code executes), large_assets (whole-map transport only),
    and the integration gap (nothing reachable from main.dart executes them).
  transfer, retry_resume, restore, conflicts, workspace_boundaries are drilled
  against the contracts that do ship and are reported as satisfied locally.
  All external gates remain DEFERRED-EXTERNAL. Release cut = operator decision.

